WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.320
Bad dudes, the forces of good have never been so bad.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:28.020
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:29.800
I'm Mike. I'm Bad.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:31.760
And I'm Joe.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.300
Guys, are you bad enough dudes to record a podcast?

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.820
I'm Bad. Sean is.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.560
Sean is. Yes.

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.340
You know, obviously it's Bad Dudes.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:45.120
Obviously that's like one of the biggest memes to ever come out of the NES.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:50.520
But realistically, forget the memes, forget the jokes, forget the whole like president's been kidnapped for a minute.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:01:03.980
This game is like so many movies and yet no no movie maker has ever made a bad dudes movie, you know, with like the rock and Vin Diesel teaming up to do the bad dudes.

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.260
Like we need that.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:06.400
Right. We need that movie.

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:15.460
Yeah. I mean, I wouldn't be surprised if you told me that this was based on some like some unknown movie that like kind of got buried by all the other similar movies.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:22.400
I'd say that this is this was turned into a movie with like Olympus has fallen.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:24.100
Oh, OK.

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:27.860
I like that. So even though it's not bad dudes, the idea.

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.240
Yeah. Yeah. He's a he is a bad dude, though.

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:32.500
Right. And this is a Data East game.

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:42.200
And in a lot of ways, Data East does make like B level movies, but for video games, you know, like the plots aren't really all that there.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:46.140
They're just they're just there to to hold the gameplay together in some kind of glue format.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:50.940
And it mostly follows like whatever Arnold Schwarzenegger was doing at the time.

00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:51.920
They just do it again.

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:56.480
So in a way, this is like a video game movie.

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:58.060
I really love that.

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:00.220
Like in some kind of glue format.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:03.860
I don't really know what it means, but I feel it.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:05.240
I feel that it's true.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:08.120
They're like they're barely story.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.280
Yeah. That'll be a next trivia question.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:14.000
Mike, did you ever say in some glue format?

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.480
I'm writing it down.

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:23.940
You know, what's funny is, is like, I guess, you know, Sean, even if you didn't know what I meant, it's Data East doesn't have the best reputation for it.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:25.100
No, no, they don't.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:28.880
So, you know, we're going to give bad dudes a fair shot here.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:44.680
And the only way to really do that is to forget about the, you know, the historical memes and the reception of the game itself and what people talk about today and just jump into the game with no, you know, with no prior knowledge of it.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:03:01.000
So if you're just joining us and you're playing as the bad dudes, Blade and Striker, you would need to know that the dudes have been tasked with rescuing the president who, depending on, you know, which game, if you're in the arcade, it's Ronald Reagan.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:05.000
If you're in the NES, I think it's Bush.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:06.680
It kind of looks like him, right?

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:07.840
They never say Bush.

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:09.420
Pretty much Bush. Yeah.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:12.260
But he hasn't just been kidnapped by Russia.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:14.620
He hasn't been kidnapped by aliens.

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:16.160
These are ninjas.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:21.060
And I'm not sure why, like, the ninjas are an organization now.

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:26.900
Like, I'm not sure when they rose to prominence and, like, we all of a sudden had a ninja terrorism watch.

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:27.780
But they've done it.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.440
They have kidnapped the president.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:36.240
And only Blade and Striker can rescue him by going through six beat-em-up levels.

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:39.820
And, you know, you just wipe your way through the enemies.

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:46.080
Unlike most beat-em-ups, though, the stage doesn't scroll after you beat all the enemies on the screen.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:50.460
You can constantly keep moving forward, which is an interesting twist on the beat-em-up genre here.

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.400
Makes it almost like a platformer.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:04:18.760
To back you up a little bit about, like, the premise of the game, about, you know, the ninja problem, if all we had to go by, if some future archaeologists were to dig up games in the 80s, games in the 90s, I feel like there would be an idea that ninjas as terrorists or ninjas as a crime problem was a real problem.

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:23.100
Because it seems to be really only an 80s thing.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.060
Well, were you alive in 1989?

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.740
Not yet. Maybe there were a lot of ninjas.

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.220
Yeah, I mean, I don't know.

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:39.720
And the fact that they're the antagonist of what seems to be a lot of video game media of the time, like, maybe that is the case.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:52.940
Yeah. Well, also, to talk about the sort of the plot here, the fact that the president or these ninjas have a helicopter waiting to take the president away.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:54.020
Am I missing something?

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:55.860
Why aren't they just taking the president away?

00:04:57.380 --> 00:04:58.480
What are they waiting for?

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:02.580
Like, a ninja? Does it just take, like, a long time to get that thing in the air?

00:05:02.800 --> 00:05:03.980
Like a really old helicopter?

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.660
You gotta, like, start it up like a lawnmower?

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:14.580
Yeah, I'm still stuck on the idea that the ninjas could successfully do something like kidnapping the president.

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:16.120
You know, something that's never been done.

00:05:16.220 --> 00:05:17.160
But these are the ninjas.

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:22.200
I mean, even in the manual, the way that it describes the story to you, the president kidnapped.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:26.640
But the really bad news is that the dragon ninja is responsible.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:29.440
It's like, the bad news isn't that the president has been kidnapped.

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:31.900
It's that the dragon ninja has resurfaced.

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:36.400
Yeah, if it was Iran, if it was Russia, like, no biggie.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:37.400
We'll get him back.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:38.820
Oh, yeah. But it's the ninjas.

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:41.620
Well, yeah, because that dragon ninja, he's such a jerk.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:44.360
You don't want to give him that satisfaction of knowing he kidnapped the president.

00:05:44.620 --> 00:05:47.440
You know, that's the real deal.

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:51.600
It's emasculating. Yeah, right, right.

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:57.500
And also, they say in the manual, you know, once he gets the helicopters up in the air, you'll never see the president again.

00:05:58.360 --> 00:05:59.400
They're not killing him or anything.

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:00.540
They're just getting him up in the air.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.000
It's like, well, he's up in the air now.

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:04.900
All those memories that we could have had.

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:06.660
The helicopter is heading right to the sun.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:08.880
Yeah, it just keeps going up.

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:14.340
All right. Sorry, I just wanted to riff on the plot a little bit.

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:15.880
No, it's true.

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:20.220
It's funny. It's also not, like, expanded upon beyond that.

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:23.420
Like, we got a lot out of the beginning of the game.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:27.040
Like, the idea that the president had been kidnapped, and we really stretched that idea.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:37.180
But now, like, for the rest of the game, there's not, like, story clues to, like, what's happening or that your whole, like, adventure could possibly take place in America.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:43.060
Like, I don't know. A lot of these locations and stuff, it's like one minute you're on a train, and then you're in, like, a jungle.

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:47.620
Like, I don't know. Maybe that's not my America, but that's what they're thinking it is.

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:49.400
That's not my America.

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:56.420
Yeah. And, you know, to comment on that, and not to bring us back to this one paragraph of the manual, but the manual does say you have to navigate your way through the city.

00:06:56.920 --> 00:06:58.840
So, like, there's just a lot of trains and forests.

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:01.260
Well, maybe this is Central Park.

00:07:01.540 --> 00:07:02.760
That's what I was going to say, yeah.

00:07:03.020 --> 00:07:06.160
Absolutely. I stand corrected. But then again, why wouldn't you be in D.C.?

00:07:07.420 --> 00:07:12.040
Well, obviously he was here to visit the U.N.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.280
Oh, that's great.

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:22.500
You know, if the Dragon Ninja can successfully kidnap the president, he can probably then get the rest of, you know, the world politic leaders.

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:24.120
World politic leaders, yes.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:27.620
There you go. Yeah, I mean, like, you know, they all have different titles, so I wasn't going to say the other presidents.

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:34.080
So it's six levels, all in the beat-em-up style of games.

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:39.900
As I was saying, it's not something where you have to take out all the enemies and then the screen scrolls forward.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:41.920
This is something where you can constantly move forward.

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:44.060
So you don't necessarily have to take down every enemy.

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:46.000
It's probably advised because they'll follow you.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:57.600
But, you know, the only thing that really changes from level to level is the environment and, you know, how many enemies they'll sick on you.

00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:07.980
But before we talk about, you know, just the levels and stuff like that, the characters you play as, the bad dudes, Blade and Striker, you pretty much can only play as Blade.

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:10.720
Striker is just for two-player, I think.

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:15.800
And even two-player won't let you play as them together, which I think is a mistake.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:20.160
The game probably, not even just from, like, you know, forget about it.

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:23.920
It would be easier if you were both playing the game, you know, with, like, a friend or something at the same time.

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:25.500
You could take down the ninjas together.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:30.080
It's also just called bad dudes and you never get to see them in action together.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:31.120
And I think that's a mistake.

00:08:31.900 --> 00:08:35.400
Controlling Blade and Striker, though, guys, what did you think about these characters?

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:39.860
I thought, like, they felt pretty responsive.

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:42.820
I do have a question for you guys.

00:08:43.600 --> 00:08:48.320
It does tie in to the controls, but this is more about the genre of it.

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:51.520
We call this a beat-em-up.

00:08:51.760 --> 00:08:56.580
Like, it's called a beat-em-up in, like, I guess, general parlance.

00:08:56.580 --> 00:09:02.260
But, like, when I think of beat-em-ups, I think of, like, what you were describing before, Mike.

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:07.680
Like, you get a handful of enemies that you have to dispatch before you can move forward.

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:11.740
Usually, these enemies take several hits to get rid of.

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:14.000
Yes, it's melee.

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:21.500
But this, I would almost describe more as just, like, a melee side-scroller than I would a beat-em-up.

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:28.080
Like, is there any other actual difference between the two?

00:09:28.160 --> 00:09:30.520
Well, I'm just thinking about it like this, you know.

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:36.720
The entirety of the game, the sole objective is just to keep attacking the enemies in front of you.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:37.960
There are no collectibles.

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:41.840
There is no, you know, the points don't do anything other than keep a high score.

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:44.440
So, you know, even platforming.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:50.780
Yes, this is an unusual choice for this game as well, where it's a flat 2D field,

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:54.840
but it has an upper and lower section to it, so you can constantly switch behind that.

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:57.220
But that's not puzzle-like.

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:00.480
It's either just, do I want to be on the top with all these enemies,

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:03.780
or do I want to go down and escape from them, but then enemies will appear down here.

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:06.740
So I'd say for the most part, I'd still put it in that beat-em-up genre,

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:11.000
just because the whole, like, idea of just beating up everything in front of you,

00:10:11.020 --> 00:10:16.860
like, that's the only thing you have to do is just keep using your fists and your feet at all times.

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:21.880
Sometimes it, um, I'm not sure if it could be anything else.

00:10:22.020 --> 00:10:22.840
I buy that.

00:10:23.500 --> 00:10:27.420
And I think that, um, there are other games that I've always considered beat-em-ups,

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:31.900
like the TMNT games, other than the one we played, but all the other 2D TMNT games,

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:34.980
where you are, yeah, you stop on the screen, you have to beat all the enemies,

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:38.400
but then, like, as you're walking, you're walking for a while and fighting people,

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:40.000
and the screen's not stopping.

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:42.780
And I think there's a lot of other beat-em-ups that kind of, like, do both.

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:48.700
Yeah. And it's a little harder to, to, to notice, because it doesn't happen as often,

00:10:48.740 --> 00:10:52.680
but it does happen in this game sometimes, where, maybe it's not where the screen's scrolling,

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:56.180
but the screen will scroll down sometimes after you, well, in later levels,

00:10:56.780 --> 00:10:57.920
after you beat up all the enemies.

00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:02.840
And then, like, once in a while, these, like, pseudo-bosses show up,

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:05.880
and you have to, you have to face them before the screen scrolls.

00:11:05.980 --> 00:11:09.440
So it's like, I don't know, it's like a fuzzy line of where to, where to draw it.

00:11:09.520 --> 00:11:12.160
But yeah, I'd also say, like, this just felt very beat-em-up to me.

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:18.460
Okay. There's also, you know, there's the two train levels that do kind of make it more

00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:20.940
Yeah. in the beat-em-up world, just because, you know,

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:22.020
You don't control it.

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:24.780
Right. It's an auto-scroller, so it's not quite the same.

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:28.320
You don't have to defeat everybody, but more enemies will just continue to come,

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:31.660
and you'll just continue to get whacked if you choose to ignore everybody.

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:35.600
Gotta get whacked. The ninjas, you know, and they're, they're doing the mafia now.

00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:37.400
Yeah, yeah.

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:40.420
Well, if it's the mafia, it's fine, but if it's the ninjas, that's the worst news.

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:42.900
Everybody, yeah, I mean, the government's done that before.

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:43.800
They've worked with the mafia.

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:46.740
Yeah. But they never worked with ninjas on record.

00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:51.640
But to go back to your original question about how, how the game controls.

00:11:52.340 --> 00:11:54.260
Yes, blade and strikers specifically.

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:58.580
All right. Well, it can only speak to the one that it defaults to.

00:11:58.800 --> 00:11:59.660
There's no difference.

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:06.360
Okay. Um, I, I think like the, his movement looks a little funny.

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:11.400
Like the, his sprites for walking are just like, he's, he's trying to walk intentionally

00:12:11.400 --> 00:12:14.220
macho, which I guess is, which I guess is cool.

00:12:14.840 --> 00:12:21.000
Um, but like when you, when you're inputting for, for jumps or for, uh, attacks, like it's,

00:12:21.060 --> 00:12:28.740
it's responsive. I never really understood like what I was doing differently to make him punch or kick or in

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:33.480
whatever sequence, um, I did find out pretty late.

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:38.820
It actually took till my second playthrough to, to do like a long press, like power punch.

00:12:39.020 --> 00:12:40.420
I didn't know that that was a thing.

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:45.460
Um, for the, for the first several, for the first like hour that I played.

00:12:46.500 --> 00:12:54.320
Um, and then, uh, the whole like jump kicks, uh, were pretty, um, satisfying to pull off.

00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:58.580
This is also, I didn't really read the manual for this one, so I'm sure they're all described,

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:03.640
but, um, uh, all in all it, it didn't feel frustrating to play.

00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:10.560
Yeah. I think that he feels, uh, like he has very heavy steps, like you said, but it does like

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:14.200
the, so I, you know, before I played it, I watched some footage of it.

00:13:14.280 --> 00:13:17.440
I was just like looking at what this game was and I was like, wow, this is going to be one

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:22.160
of those games that really feels like, like it drags to, to move.

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:24.080
And it actually doesn't feel that bad.

00:13:24.220 --> 00:13:29.160
It does feel like intentionally they want him to feel like this big, big, like, yeah,

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:33.680
like heavier guy who like isn't nimble and quick like other characters.

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:34.660
So that felt intentional.

00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:41.960
Um, I'll say that I, I think sometimes with the jumping, I mean, I guess by the way he moves,

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:42.820
that feels fine.

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:48.960
But by the way, the jumping input works was frustrating to me quite a bit where just to

00:13:48.960 --> 00:13:51.140
give you like the quick, the quick idea of it.

00:13:51.380 --> 00:13:56.960
You, if you press B, you jump, but if you press B and up, you'll jump up a really high.

00:13:57.060 --> 00:14:00.340
And that's really what you need to use to jump over attacks or to jump from like one level

00:14:00.340 --> 00:14:04.840
to another. And I'd say that that worked for me like 50% of the time, like, like you just got to get

00:14:04.840 --> 00:14:07.800
it exactly at the same moment or else you'll just do a regular jump.

00:14:07.940 --> 00:14:13.680
And that was contributed to a lot of my health loss is that I was trying to jump over something

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:17.400
and, or I was trying to jump up to the next level and I missed it and then I got hit.

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:20.660
Now, Joe, you mentioned that it's B to jump.

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:24.940
Did you guys notice that that is a swap from what we are used to?

00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:29.960
Like I, I did not, to be honest, like I just, I, I read the inputs, right?

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:32.820
Like as I, as I'm playing the game, I just say, okay, this button does that, that button

00:14:32.820 --> 00:14:35.860
does that. And then like for my game, that's just how it is.

00:14:35.940 --> 00:14:38.760
Like, I don't think about it from one game to another.

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:42.920
Whenever I go back, you know, and I play games across all different consoles, just, you know,

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:46.620
you just relearn the controls when you go back to the game or if you've played it enough,

00:14:46.640 --> 00:14:53.840
you just know them. This one, you know, it's a, they, they make a point to call it out in, um, in most websites

00:14:53.840 --> 00:14:59.080
that, you know, every other game has A to jump and B to attack and this has switched them.

00:14:59.300 --> 00:15:04.240
To be honest, it didn't, it wasn't jarring to me at all, but, uh, now noticing that I wonder

00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:09.100
why, uh, they went against what every other game was doing now that they've pointed it

00:15:09.100 --> 00:15:10.820
out. Yeah, that is weird.

00:15:10.860 --> 00:15:17.560
I also didn't notice, um, mostly because, uh, if it were a, uh, if this were a game on

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:23.880
like the PlayStation or the Xbox or something with several, with several more buttons, it

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:28.400
might have been more of like a, huh, I wonder why they didn't go with like the, the general

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:35.140
practice. But since it's just the two buttons, uh, it took me a second and, uh, it felt normal

00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:40.400
from there. To bring up a familiar game, uh, Final Fantasy VII has that problem, right?

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:42.480
Where like... Well, that's most Japanese games.

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:48.400
Right, right. Where they're switched and it's, and it's, you know, it's, it's a problem for like a minute

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:49.700
and then you just get used to it.

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:56.000
Exactly. And then once you switch it to like, where we're talking about circle being confirmed and

00:15:56.000 --> 00:16:04.840
X being, uh, back or no, um, cancel, um, and then it, it being switched between a lot

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:06.280
of Japanese and American titles.

00:16:06.480 --> 00:16:11.680
Uh, but then if I play Final Fantasy VII and like remap the controls to X being confirmed,

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:13.100
it just feels wrong.

00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:18.960
You guys covered it pretty well, all the different kinds of attacks they can do, but I think that's

00:16:18.960 --> 00:16:20.120
a lot for two buttons.

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:26.280
I was surprised that they even have for the, um, the jump kick, it's just a normal flying

00:16:26.280 --> 00:16:29.000
kick or it, it has to do with timing.

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:30.900
I'm not quite sure what the timing is.

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:34.780
Maybe it's just being fast between jumping and then the attack button.

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:39.020
Maybe that makes it land better, but you can do a spinning jump kick without having to like

00:16:39.020 --> 00:16:40.620
fiddle with the D-pad at all.

00:16:40.720 --> 00:16:41.920
It's just based on your timing.

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:45.980
And I thought that was another nice touch too, to have all these different kinds of attacks

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:50.220
where I found the attacks lacking was where the hitbox was in this game.

00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:55.160
Um, not that it's impossible by any means, but it took me a lot of learning to remember

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:57.940
that I need to be close to these guys.

00:16:57.980 --> 00:17:02.460
And I found myself through my first couple of playthroughs, always getting these like

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:06.360
dreamlike punches, you know, where you're like, you're, you feel like you're touching

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:08.380
their face, but you're not touching their face.

00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:10.520
And so therefore nothing happens, but they hit you.

00:17:10.740 --> 00:17:13.580
I was surprised that that happened to me a lot, uh, throughout this game.

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:17.460
It's something that you just learn, uh, that you have to be close to the enemies.

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:20.760
I didn't find that to be ideal because obviously the closer you get to the enemies, the more

00:17:20.760 --> 00:17:22.600
likely they are to attack you as well.

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:28.480
So if you have a storm of, you know, five or six ninjas on you, it's going to be, it's

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:32.320
going to be tough to, uh, deal with all of them at once in close range.

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:36.960
So I did find myself gradually losing health throughout these levels because of that decision.

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:41.320
But I wasn't sure if that hitbox also was something you guys know.

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:49.720
Um, when it, when it came to fighting on fighting enemies that were on the same level as me, uh,

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:52.520
I don't think I ran into it as much as you did.

00:17:52.700 --> 00:18:00.340
It did still happen, but where I think the, the biggest, uh, disparity, uh, was cause there's

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:04.280
a whole like subgroup of enemies that they just attack you from above.

00:18:04.460 --> 00:18:08.080
They'll jump and then they'll try and land on you with like a sword pointing down.

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:15.100
Uh, unless you're right below them, uh, your upward attack, I felt like missed half the

00:18:15.100 --> 00:18:18.800
time. And then I would take damage from that and then they jump up again and I'd have to

00:18:18.800 --> 00:18:26.240
try again. Uh, so in that specific instance, I felt like hitboxes were a little wonky, but in general,

00:18:26.500 --> 00:18:30.660
I, I guess I just ended up being close enough, enough times.

00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:34.820
It's funny because I feel like we all, all three of us noticed like totally different

00:18:34.820 --> 00:18:39.880
things that, that we liked and that bothered us because I didn't, I didn't notice.

00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:44.320
I do now that you mentioned it, Mike, I didn't notice the, the, the hitboxes being weird,

00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:46.060
but now that you mentioned it, yes, they, they were.

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:51.340
Um, and then as far as the, uh, the jumping, the, the enemies that would jump down, I just

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:55.080
had to use a different strategy on them where I would just step to the side and like duck

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:56.200
and hit them as they land.

00:18:56.920 --> 00:19:01.380
So like they didn't bother me, but what bothered me was the fact that, yeah, there's all this

00:19:01.380 --> 00:19:04.780
like, there's all this variety of attacks and punching and spin kicks.

00:19:04.960 --> 00:19:07.560
I never felt any need to use any of that.

00:19:08.260 --> 00:19:13.500
My, all I did was take a nunchuck once I had them and just bop everyone in the face once.

00:19:13.980 --> 00:19:16.560
Like that was just, I felt like the easiest way to do anything.

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:19.680
So it's like, yeah, there's all this other stuff, but like none of it really worked for

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:22.220
me that much or it would usually lead to me losing more health.

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:27.380
And I'm not saying it was necessarily easy, but it was the easiest to just, to just use

00:19:27.380 --> 00:19:32.580
the nunchuck. And that was like a little uninteresting to me sometimes enemies coming from all directions

00:19:32.580 --> 00:19:35.280
coming everywhere. And it was just hit this one, hit that one, hit this one, hit that one.

00:19:35.420 --> 00:19:39.220
Like even some of the bosses, there's, there's that boss that multiplies himself to a bunch

00:19:39.220 --> 00:19:42.680
of people. And like, that should be like cool and interesting and hard.

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:44.000
And it's really not that hard.

00:19:44.020 --> 00:19:46.180
You just give them a couple of one by one.

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:48.400
Yeah. Like literally they like line up.

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:49.500
You just hit them as they come.

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:51.700
As long as you just hit them before they get too close to you.

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:53.320
They're not going to hurt you.

00:19:53.600 --> 00:19:55.000
And then you fight the boss.

00:19:55.160 --> 00:20:00.780
Like, I don't know. I noticed that a lot in this game where at first I was like, oh, okay, this is, this is

00:20:00.780 --> 00:20:01.940
fun. It controls nicely.

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:05.320
And after a while I was like, okay, am I just, I'm just doing the same thing over and

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:06.460
over again with like no variety.

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:10.060
And like, yes, there's variety in the game, but I didn't have any incentive to do it.

00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:13.880
And the power-ups that you're talking about, you know, the nunchucks and the sword and,

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:17.800
and I think otherwise it's just a clock and an energy can, right?

00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:25.380
Yeah. Those power-ups, it's a different style for beat-em-ups than what we've seen with like

00:20:25.380 --> 00:20:27.980
Double Dragon, a game that we put on the essential games list.

00:20:28.180 --> 00:20:34.000
Double Dragon made it so that there were environmental weapons that you could pick up, but also that

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:36.520
enemies could pick up and you could use those to attack.

00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:41.720
And I don't remember if they broke or not or whatever, but they didn't last for long or

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:46.940
anything like that. And in this game instead, power-ups are just, they're not environmental, they're dropped.

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:52.460
And you still have to do the action of picking them up or whatever, but then they stay with

00:20:52.460 --> 00:20:53.780
you until you die, correct?

00:20:54.440 --> 00:20:55.460
Yes. Yeah.

00:20:56.700 --> 00:20:58.840
So it's a different, it's a different decision.

00:20:59.560 --> 00:21:01.060
And it's like twofold for me.

00:21:01.240 --> 00:21:02.800
One, I'm not sure if that was the right choice.

00:21:02.820 --> 00:21:08.080
I think a lot of fun, especially in later beat-em-ups or in arcade beat-em-ups are the

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:09.020
environmental stuff.

00:21:09.300 --> 00:21:12.800
This game is kind of bare, even on the platforming.

00:21:12.940 --> 00:21:18.580
When you think about, you know, the fact that they made it so this way there's a top and

00:21:18.580 --> 00:21:22.740
a bottom level at all times, they didn't do anything cool about that really.

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:27.180
I never found myself in a situation where I was like, oh, I could trick a bunch of enemies

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:28.020
by doing this.

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:32.480
You know, the only thing I could think of is in the train stages, sometimes if you go to

00:21:32.480 --> 00:21:35.340
the bottom, you're on the track now and you're dead.

00:21:35.340 --> 00:21:40.080
You know, like that was only like the only example I could think of, you know, something

00:21:40.080 --> 00:21:41.660
different for the two platforms.

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:47.000
Otherwise, it was just a reason to dodge enemies, which could be enough for some people, but it

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:53.280
wasn't enough for me. And also the only two power-ups doesn't feel like it's taking full advantage of what the

00:21:53.280 --> 00:21:54.260
bad dudes could do.

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:59.880
I mean, these guys have a fist that they could turn into like a fire punch and zap it at people.

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:02.620
But then meanwhile, there's no power-up cooler than that.

00:22:02.780 --> 00:22:03.640
It's just nunchucks.

00:22:04.640 --> 00:22:05.580
Yeah, I don't know.

00:22:05.780 --> 00:22:09.200
I think there are a lot of instances like that where like they just didn't fully take advantage

00:22:09.200 --> 00:22:12.940
of stuff they had in there. But like the train thing that you mentioned, I thought was a really cool thing that we

00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:16.920
hadn't seen because you land on the bottom and you kind of move towards the right of

00:22:16.920 --> 00:22:20.720
the screen because the train's going to the left like you're on the ground and the platform

00:22:20.720 --> 00:22:23.180
is moving above you. But like, that's really it.

00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:24.340
You just shouldn't be down there.

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:26.980
Like I thought it was like, oh, maybe there's incentive to be down there and it's a little

00:22:26.980 --> 00:22:28.400
harder. It's like, nah, just don't go down there.

00:22:28.400 --> 00:22:33.000
Yeah, they could have done something really annoying where like in a train level, you have

00:22:33.000 --> 00:22:38.100
to be down to the bottom platform, which would just be like the side of the train because

00:22:38.100 --> 00:22:41.880
now you're going through a tunnel and like anybody on the top half gets like killed,

00:22:42.120 --> 00:22:45.040
you know? Yeah, yeah. So you have to be dodging for that reason.

00:22:45.220 --> 00:22:47.080
I would have liked to have seen some more stuff like that.

00:22:47.160 --> 00:22:49.280
It doesn't have to be restricted to the auto-scrolling stages.

00:22:49.700 --> 00:22:54.540
I'm just surprised that there wasn't even, you know, not puzzles, but there just wasn't

00:22:54.540 --> 00:22:57.020
any kind of platforming use for that.

00:22:57.220 --> 00:23:00.020
You know, it's like they just had that idea, but they didn't really have like a good reason

00:23:00.020 --> 00:23:05.600
to implement it or they didn't come up with like, I don't know, any game mechanics that

00:23:05.600 --> 00:23:06.740
really complement it.

00:23:19.700 --> 00:23:23.980
What about the variety of the enemies or even just the variety of the levels?

00:23:24.480 --> 00:23:27.860
We've been talking a lot about the difference between the auto-scrolling and regular stages,

00:23:28.300 --> 00:23:33.960
but is this a game where once you've played the first level, you've experienced the game

00:23:33.960 --> 00:23:38.860
or does the game progress and evolve in other ways other than just difficulty?

00:23:39.540 --> 00:23:47.720
Um, I'd say that there is some different variety of like the kinds of enemies that you fight.

00:23:47.820 --> 00:23:55.360
Like when you get to the later levels, you've got like what Joe was saying earlier, like

00:23:55.360 --> 00:24:02.440
those sub-boss guys that they're just big and they're not, they're not like special in

00:24:02.440 --> 00:24:06.060
any way, but they do take more hits.

00:24:06.060 --> 00:24:13.560
Uh, you've got some enemies that are kind of like bosses that are now just mobs, like you,

00:24:13.740 --> 00:24:17.460
like the guys that turn, that turn into like several versions of them.

00:24:17.700 --> 00:24:22.560
There's not a lot of variety, um, that, that like, that evolves.

00:24:22.860 --> 00:24:27.280
A lot of it is the same kind of variety from the first level, but I'd say that like, uh,

00:24:27.280 --> 00:24:35.700
between different stage, uh, stage construction and, uh, the addition of these few different

00:24:35.700 --> 00:24:41.740
kinds of enemies, there is some variety, but yeah, the first level, you're kind of, you're

00:24:41.740 --> 00:24:43.480
kind of get the most out of it.

00:24:43.600 --> 00:24:46.340
You're seeing what this game kind of has to offer.

00:24:47.380 --> 00:24:51.580
Yeah. As far as the, yeah, as far as that variety, I think that like some of the stuff that it

00:24:51.580 --> 00:24:55.100
offers are with the one, you know, the one we talked about where the guy jumps up with

00:24:55.100 --> 00:24:55.900
a sword and comes down.

00:24:56.040 --> 00:24:57.620
You have to think about that in a different way.

00:24:57.860 --> 00:25:03.760
Then there are these like putty looking things from a power rangers that, that throw, throw

00:25:03.760 --> 00:25:04.980
throwing stars at you.

00:25:05.160 --> 00:25:07.560
You know, you have to think about those in a different way because you've got to like jump

00:25:07.560 --> 00:25:08.560
their, their attack.

00:25:09.140 --> 00:25:13.840
And then there are a bunch of other ones that also do different things, but like, I don't

00:25:13.840 --> 00:25:17.580
really remember too much of what they all do because my solution to all of them are

00:25:17.580 --> 00:25:20.400
another just bop in the face with the, with the nunchucks.

00:25:20.560 --> 00:25:23.180
Like, like I see that they, that they do different things.

00:25:23.320 --> 00:25:24.220
They, they have different weapons.

00:25:24.340 --> 00:25:25.180
They shoot different things.

00:25:25.340 --> 00:25:28.000
There's, you know, one of them ducks.

00:25:28.580 --> 00:25:31.260
So you have to duck and then bop them in the face with your nunchucks.

00:25:31.360 --> 00:25:32.660
So it's like, oh, that's a little different.

00:25:32.800 --> 00:25:36.940
But for the most part, like, I think a lot of the variety ends up falling into this like

00:25:38.420 --> 00:25:40.460
same method of defeating them.

00:25:40.860 --> 00:25:43.820
Um, other than those few little things where like there's a guy who's not

00:25:43.820 --> 00:25:45.800
on fire who you have to jump over.

00:25:46.080 --> 00:25:47.500
Yeah. But like, I forgot about that.

00:25:48.080 --> 00:25:49.940
Yeah. That's really random too.

00:25:50.040 --> 00:25:52.160
It's like the only person like that in the game.

00:25:52.380 --> 00:25:55.660
Well, that's the guy from a teenage mutant Ninja turtles fire.

00:25:55.900 --> 00:26:00.640
Right. He left the foot clan and now he's joined the dragon Ninja clan.

00:26:00.920 --> 00:26:03.300
Yeah. He left the history of all the comics too.

00:26:03.820 --> 00:26:05.220
Right. Yeah, absolutely.

00:26:05.940 --> 00:26:10.340
I guess my point here that, you know, and I'm not trying to like beat up specifically

00:26:10.340 --> 00:26:12.500
on, um, bad dudes here.

00:26:12.500 --> 00:26:15.820
There are other video games that have this problem too, specifically for the NES that

00:26:15.820 --> 00:26:22.600
we played. There's a, there's a certain point with these games as opposed to, you know, now we have

00:26:22.600 --> 00:26:27.740
these story driven games on, um, you know, on PS5 and Xbox one, but we've been having

00:26:27.740 --> 00:26:28.840
them for a long time.

00:26:29.400 --> 00:26:34.220
Story driven games have this promise of like, okay, well, even if you are doing the same

00:26:34.220 --> 00:26:37.400
thing over and over again, it's like now it's like reading a book.

00:26:37.480 --> 00:26:39.440
It's like, okay, but you get the next chapter of the tale.

00:26:39.440 --> 00:26:41.020
You get a reason to move forward.

00:26:41.540 --> 00:26:43.800
These NES games don't always have that.

00:26:43.920 --> 00:26:49.600
And this one specifically does not where there's, there's not really a sense of, of progress or,

00:26:49.600 --> 00:26:51.880
uh, you know, your skill increasing.

00:26:52.580 --> 00:26:58.400
There is a point where you could become someone like Joe, who is, you know, an awesome bad

00:26:58.400 --> 00:27:03.520
dude, a guy who can clearly take down anybody with his nunchucks, but it just becomes a very

00:27:03.520 --> 00:27:08.880
repetitive thing that like, you know, God forbid you lose those nunchucks.

00:27:09.040 --> 00:27:13.920
You're probably also going to lose your interest in the game too, because now it's just a matter

00:27:13.920 --> 00:27:17.900
of either picking them up again or surviving, uh, to get to the end.

00:27:17.900 --> 00:27:19.500
Dude, not enough is changing.

00:27:19.740 --> 00:27:24.760
Yeah. Um, in a lot of these games where you actually feel like, you know, oh dude, but wait till

00:27:24.760 --> 00:27:28.940
you get to level six, you know, like that it's never going, no one's going to say that

00:27:28.940 --> 00:27:32.080
about bad dudes. Nothing changes, uh, within it.

00:27:32.200 --> 00:27:37.980
Whereas, you know, most of our essential games, uh, things like Mega Man, you play like a whole

00:27:37.980 --> 00:27:42.640
first part of a game and then it's like, okay, thank you for playing like the base game.

00:27:42.640 --> 00:27:48.020
Now here's the actual game where you take everything you've learned and, uh, go through, you know,

00:27:48.080 --> 00:27:53.640
the gauntlet with refighting all the bosses and fighting new bosses and, uh, solving more

00:27:53.640 --> 00:27:55.200
interesting puzzles and platforms.

00:27:56.020 --> 00:28:01.020
This game, like, like a lot of games, but also like a lot of arcade games just continues

00:28:01.020 --> 00:28:06.020
to offer you the same thing where your only objective is just, can you survive to the finish?

00:28:06.020 --> 00:28:13.280
Yeah. I think like one thing that, uh, games like this and, and even the arcade versions of them,

00:28:13.460 --> 00:28:23.940
uh, would use as sort of like, uh, uh, a reason to keep going is, uh, like the, the settings,

00:28:24.020 --> 00:28:28.620
like the level actual, like the backgrounds of, of this stuff, like where you're fighting.

00:28:28.900 --> 00:28:33.860
Um, and this is a pretty good looking game in terms of its sprites and its backgrounds.

00:28:33.860 --> 00:28:40.080
Uh, the only problem is that the most like interesting places that you, that you actually play bad

00:28:40.080 --> 00:28:42.080
dudes are like pretty front loaded.

00:28:42.460 --> 00:28:48.380
Um, in the, at near the end of the game, you're fighting in a sewer, a cave and in some like

00:28:48.380 --> 00:28:55.100
really generic looking military complex and like all the cool stuff, like the streets of

00:28:55.100 --> 00:29:00.800
New York and, uh, uh, on the highway, uh, like all that's pretty early.

00:29:00.800 --> 00:29:05.880
And I know that that's a pretty like weak reason, um, to say like, Oh, I'll just keep

00:29:05.880 --> 00:29:10.680
playing because I, I like the, the, the window dressing and a lot of stuff, but I still think

00:29:10.680 --> 00:29:14.260
it's, it could be a reason to keep playing.

00:29:14.740 --> 00:29:20.600
Uh, but yeah, that other than that, nothing else, nothing else is really evolving here.

00:29:20.740 --> 00:29:24.140
I think that the window dressing is, is at least a factor, right?

00:29:24.140 --> 00:29:30.800
Right. Yeah. And that coupled with the fact that, that the gameplay just doesn't, doesn't get any

00:29:30.800 --> 00:29:36.040
different really. In fact, I think in some cases, I'm sure we'll talk about this later, but in some cases I

00:29:36.040 --> 00:29:37.240
think the gameplay gets a little easier.

00:29:37.240 --> 00:29:40.780
I think some of the early boss battles are harder than some of the later boss battles.

00:29:41.000 --> 00:29:44.660
Weird, weird stuff, but granted I didn't finish the game, so maybe it gets harder again,

00:29:44.820 --> 00:29:49.980
but, but yeah, I think that like all those things together make it feel like you're going

00:29:49.980 --> 00:29:51.040
to lose interest after a bit.

00:29:55.080 --> 00:29:58.360
Well, since you brought it up, Joe, I think now would be a great time to talk about those

00:29:58.360 --> 00:30:04.260
boss fights. Um, they are the noticeable difference in, in your enemies, right?

00:30:04.300 --> 00:30:07.040
It's not just more ninjas coming at you in giant waves.

00:30:07.160 --> 00:30:11.840
Instead, now you finally have the big bad at the end of the level, which, um, you know,

00:30:11.940 --> 00:30:16.500
we're not strangers to by any means, but we're not strangers to the very first boss in this

00:30:16.500 --> 00:30:17.620
game. Karnoff.

00:30:17.800 --> 00:30:23.320
Yeah. Uh, the guy, the guy from who got his own game, uh, a while back, obviously also a data

00:30:23.320 --> 00:30:25.700
East game surprised to see him here.

00:30:25.800 --> 00:30:31.360
He looks a little bit different, but, um, he was, he, he was an interesting boss.

00:30:31.360 --> 00:30:36.280
If only just because his jump had this weird thing where I felt like I couldn't avoid it

00:30:36.280 --> 00:30:37.620
unless I was on a separate platform.

00:30:37.620 --> 00:30:39.780
Like him jumping over you is an attack.

