here's all these extra features, or here's this new thing.

00:46:57.580 --> 00:47:01.100
I really feel like even though I don't usually play two-player mode,

00:47:01.100 --> 00:47:09.100
something like being able to play as Blade and Striker simultaneously would have been, like, a bigger sell for a game called Bad Dudes,

00:47:09.100 --> 00:47:12.100
or, you know, even being able to switch between them.

00:47:12.220 --> 00:47:16.280
Like, they tag in and tag out, and you have to manage their health or something.

00:47:17.240 --> 00:47:21.520
That could have been an interesting, unique idea that the arcade version wouldn't have been able to pull off.

00:47:21.520 --> 00:47:30.300
However, instead, we just get the arcade game watered down, and I can confidently say that because I did play the arcade game,

00:47:30.380 --> 00:47:31.700
and I thought that was pretty fun.

00:47:31.700 --> 00:47:35.080
I'm not saying it's, like, one of the better arcade games, but I had a good time with that one.

00:47:35.220 --> 00:47:41.360
I didn't have as much of a good time with the NES one afterwards because I just realized I was missing most of what I enjoyed

00:47:41.840 --> 00:47:43.980
after going back to the arcade version.

00:47:43.980 --> 00:47:51.540
So this is one of those games that, like, probably gets too bad of a rap just because it was, like, considered really silly

00:47:52.060 --> 00:47:55.840
with its plot and everything, and then people, like, start playing the game because of that

00:47:55.840 --> 00:47:58.240
and realize, like, oh, wait a minute, I don't like older games.

00:47:58.300 --> 00:48:02.480
So it has, like, this additional rap as, like, a bad game that it doesn't deserve,

00:48:03.020 --> 00:48:09.100
but it really is just a game where it's, like, this was at, you know, your local pizzeria or your local arcade or whatever,

00:48:09.600 --> 00:48:12.960
and now you wanted to just own it rather than continue to spend quarters,

00:48:12.960 --> 00:48:16.420
and you saw it at, you know, your local video game store, and you were like,

00:48:16.480 --> 00:48:18.400
cool, now I can play this in my living room.

00:48:18.400 --> 00:48:20.180
So you bought it for that reason.

00:48:20.380 --> 00:48:23.700
I don't think this is a game that necessarily holds up for any other reason,

00:48:23.700 --> 00:48:25.580
so I can't put it on the list for that.

